# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. On a host such as Netlify, Vercel
# or Cloudflare Pages, set the same variables in the project settings.
#
# Nothing needs to be set. Left empty, both forms open the visitor's mail
# program addressed to the email in src/data/site.ts
# (adefemi@runeward.io), with the message filled in. They press send there.
#
# To send a form somewhere else, set its variable to one of:
#
#   mailto:...    Another email address, for example mailto:you@example.com.
#   https://...   A form service that accepts a JSON POST and answers with
#                 a 2xx status (for example Formspree), if you later want
#                 visitors to stay on the page instead of opening mail.
#
# "npm run dev" ignores these unless they are set: the forms then post to
# the dev server, which writes to .cache/reports.jsonl and
# .cache/subscribers.jsonl, and no mail program opens.

# "Report a problem". Fields sent: message, email (if given), page, title,
# context.
PUBLIC_REPORT_ENDPOINT=

# Newsletter sign-ups. Fields sent: email, page.
PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT=
